## Don't edit this file. OpenSSH uses the FIRST value it obtains for each option.
## To override an option per-user, use '~/.ssh/config' (read before the system
## configuration). To override system-wide, use a drop-in with a LOWER number
## than this one, such as '/etc/ssh/ssh_config.d/20_user.conf' (drop-ins are read
## in lexical order).

## See also:
## https://www.kicksecure.com/wiki/SSH#Client_Configuration_File

Host *
  ## Strictest posture, matching the server: post-quantum-only key exchange and
  ## the aes256-gcm cipher only. Outbound SSH therefore only succeeds to a
  ## post-quantum-capable server; to reach a server that offers a narrower
  ## algorithm set, override per-host in '~/.ssh/config' (SSH reads it before the
  ## system configuration, so its value wins).
  VisualHostKey yes
  Ciphers aes256-gcm@openssh.com
  MACs umac-128-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com
  KexAlgorithms sntrup761x25519-sha512,sntrup761x25519-sha512@openssh.com,mlkem768x25519-sha256
  HostKeyAlgorithms sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com,ssh-ed25519
  PubkeyAcceptedAlgorithms sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com,ssh-ed25519
